const title='DragonSword Awakening Combat System — Status Ailments & Signal Skills'; const description='Understand the DragonSword Awakening combat system: Active Skills, Status Ailments, Signal Skills, Switching Signals, team order, setup, connector and finisher roles.'; const canonical='https://dragonswordguide.com/guides/combat-system/'; const article={ '@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'Article',headline:title,description,mainEntityOfPage:canonical,datePublished:'2026-08-08',dateModified:'2026-08-08',publisher:{'@type':'Organization',name:'DragonSword Guide'} }; const sources=[{label:'Official Steam store page',href:sourceUrls.steam,note:'describes 19 Heroes, Status Ailments, Active Skills, Signal Skills and Switching Signals.'}];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} ogType="article" schema={[article]}><div class="shell page-wrap"><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'DragonSword Guide',href:'/'},{label:'Guides',href:'/guides/beginner/'},{label:'Combat System'}]} /><article><header class="article-header"><p class="eyebrow">Guide · Read the signal</p><h1>DragonSword Awakening Combat System</h1><LastVerified date="August 8, 2026" /></header><QuickAnswer title="Build the condition, then cash it in."><p>The public Steam description frames combat around stacking Status Ailments with Active Skills, then chaining Signal Skills through a three-Hero tag-team. Switching Signals are the connective tissue between those moments.</p></QuickAnswer><div class="article-body"><CombatFlow /><SectionHeader title="The five-step combat flow" /><h2>1. Active Skills</h2><p>Active Skills are the first deliberate input in the chain. Learn which skill creates the state you want before worrying about a character’s final damage numbers.</p><h2>2. Status Ailments</h2><p>Each of the 19 Heroes is described as having distinct Status Ailment abilities. Treat the ailment as a condition to read and exploit, not a reason to lock a single Hero in place.</p><h2>3. Signal Skills</h2><p>After a condition is established, use the next Hero’s Signal Skill to convert the opening into a stronger sequence. The exact pairing depends on the Hero data you have verified in your own build.</p><h2>4. Switching Signals</h2><p>Switching Signals let Heroes weave in and out of battle. This is why a team’s order is a combat decision: your setup, connector and finisher should be easy to reach.</p><h2>5. Finisher</h2><p>Finish the sequence when the status setup and signal chain have done their job. We are not publishing character-specific rotations until they are tested against the current retail build.</p><h2>Why team order matters</h2><p>A good team is legible under pressure. Put the Hero who starts your preferred condition first, keep the connector close, and reserve the last slot for the payoff you can actually execute.</p><h2>Setup, connector, finisher</h2><p>This is a useful planning language, not an official class system. It helps you compare teams without pretending the game has a fixed trinity or a definitive meta.</p></div><SourceList sources={sources}/><RelatedGuides links={[{label:'Beginner Guide',href:'/guides/beginner/'},{label:'Teams',href:'/teams/'},{label:'Characters',href:'/characters/'}]}/></article></div></BaseLayout>
